---
title: What is skoro?
summary: The problem skoro solves, who it is for, and what makes it different from other probabilistic programming libraries.
order: 1
---

Skoro is a probabilistic modeling library for Rust. You describe a model as a cascade of
conditional distributions over typed quantities (reals, vectors, matrices, rotations, rigid-body
poses and discrete values). Skoro keeps that description as a graph, and inference algorithms
can sample it, score it, differentiate it, and read its structure.

## The problem

